WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.068
-We had a great thing happen
one time when we had lunch.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were standing in
the street talking.

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, are you kidding me?
Best day of my life.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:05.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:09.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were standing in the street
talking, and we're both,

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.177
you know -- we're both
television personalities.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've --
You're a film maker.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're a very
well-known comedian.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:20.086
We were standing on the street,
and not a single person stopped.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No one said hello.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, who did we see?
-You would think that would be

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
some kind of spectacle.
These two guys.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nothing.
-And we were working it.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.794
We were standing there for
a full ten minutes talking.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Bradley Cooper
showed up.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bradley Cooper showed up.
The Bradley Cooper.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:34.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was thrilled,
because I went to college

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.837
at the same time and at the
same college as Bradley Cooper.

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:38.605 line:92%
I was in the improv group.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was in the nomadic
theatre company,

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.775 size:84% position:42%
but I never met him.
We never crossed paths.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:42.876 line:92%
We were at parties and things.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was famously good-looking.
-Oh, gotcha.

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
That didn't develop
later in life?

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but you really have
to be so good looking

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:55.355
to be good looking in --
like, famously good looking

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
in college.
-Oh, I see what you mean.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Like, in other words,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can be, like,
he's sexiest man alive,

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you can pull that con over
on a "people,"

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
but not on your English class,
you know what I mean?

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
You really have
to sell it local.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he had it!

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he really --
People would be like,

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Have you ever seen
Bradley Cooper?"

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
We never met, and then here
we are in the street,

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know Bradley,
and you introduced me to him.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.346
And I said, "Hey, I was in
the improv group you went to --

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were in the
other theater group."

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.650 line:92%
And he just goes, "All right."

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.987
And I was like, that's a --
That's a letdown, but --

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in retrospect,
I blame you, because...

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...well, because of
the introduction.

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:35.095
I feel like on this show,
you do such a nice job.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.231
This next guy is a filmmaker,
he did "Sleepwalk with Me,"

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he did the thing --
got a new tour,

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
please welcome Mike Birbiglia.
You didn't do that.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just go,
[ mumbling ] "Mike Birbiglia,"

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel like you
could have gone big!

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
You could have been like,
"This guy,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's a very small part
in 'Train Wreck,'

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
he is the 75th lead on
'Orange is the New Black,'

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was on one episode
of 'Girls,'

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
please welcome
Mike Birbiglia, everybody."

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nice to meet you.
He'd be like, "Oh, wow."

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I should have given you
a talk-show introduction.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.288
Do you remember, the other thing
that I remember happening is

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
after no one, not
a single person noticed us...

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...a very beautiful woman

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.529 size:75% position:38%
walked by and, like,
saw Bradley Cooper

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
and went into like --
Yeah, it was an Irish woman.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-It was like "The Matrix"

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
where everything got
really slow.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She was like --

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:16.469 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it's wild.
He is astoundingly beautiful.

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he really is.
And then we, like, had lunch,

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just ate in silence.
-Well, that lunch --

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.378
That lunch was very memorable
for me because I was writing

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
this movie I made called
"Don't Think Twice."

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A fantastic film.
-Oh, thanks!

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's about --

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:31.885 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:32.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thanks.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.821
If you're not familiar,
it's a film about sort of

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
a group of best friends
in an improv group,

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.892
and someone gets cast in sort of
a "Saturday Night Live"

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
type show, sort of
a doppelganger "SNL"

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a doppelganger
Lorne Michaels.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.932
I was terrified at the time that
we were just going to get sued

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
by "SNL" and Lorne Michaels,
and so then when we went

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.771
to lunch, I thought here is a
great opportunity to talk to

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
the person who is
my Lorne Michaels,

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's you.
-Oh.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:56.910 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Crowd aws ]

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Although, I don't know --
-No, I don't know.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.114 size:88% position:44% line:92%
No, I mean -- No, it is.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.716
I mean, like -- I wouldn't know
how to call Lorne.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I talked to you
to get a vibe on it,

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.255 line:92%
so I pitched you the movie.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.558 size:75% position:38% line:92%
You gave me nothing.

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.727
-And when I say nothing,
I mean precisely nothing.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.596 line:92%
Like, you didn't go positive.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.566 size:84% position:42%
You didn't go negative.
You just go, "Hmmm."

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.668
I go, "It's a movie about this,
blah, blah, blah."

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you go, "All right."
-Yeah.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.805
-And then when we were leaving,
when I was dropping you off

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.740 size:88% position:44%
at your apartment, I go,
"Hey, what do you think?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.275
Do you think Lorne would be --"
that's the thing I was

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
nervous about. "Do you think
Lorne would be okay

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
with that movie?"
And you go,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.415 size:78% position:39%
"Lorne is never going
to see your movie."

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.786 size:84% position:42%
-And that was not meant
to be cruel in any way.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It wasn't cruel.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:43.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was exactly what
I needed to hear.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:43.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.491 size:84% position:42%
There's a lot of things
I've done, and Lorne is

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:49.295
the executive producer of
this show, that he has not seen.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I'm sure.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, but you haven't heard
from him yet, right?

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.967
You haven't heard from him
about "Don't Think Twice"?

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.868
-No, no.
I think that would have been --

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, that would have been,
like, a great thing

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
if we got sued by "SNL"
in some ways.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would have been
a big publicity thing.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-We're much -- We're very low.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.245 line:92%
We're a little under the radar.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:08.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, so I'm on
this new tour that we ran

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:13.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
into each other on the flight,
and then the pod --

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
this podcast, by the way,
is my own podcast.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you --
When you were doing your --

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you put on your ear buds
to tune me out,

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.261 line:92%
you were listening to yourself.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.563 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, I mean, it's got
a lot of layers to it.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I've heard it --

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, this is --
because your new show --

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're touring a show called
"The New One."

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I don't like
to talk about it.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.372 size:78% position:39%
Like, in other words,
you know how, like,

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.307
your favorite movie is like --
My favorite movies this year are

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
like "Lady Bird" and
"The Big Sick" and "Get Out."

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:39.979
And like, what I like to do is,
to my friends I say,

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
"See this movie.
Don't see a trailer.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't see --
Don't read a review."

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-And I think that's a really

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
great gift you
can give somebody.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I don't --
With my new show,

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't tell people
anything about it.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:53.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just say, "If you like
the old albums, the old ones,

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.862
come see 'The New One'."
And so I have this five-episode

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:58.531
limited podcast where I talk to,
like, old friends --

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:01.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
John Mulaney,
Judd Apatow, Ira Glass --

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the old albums.
-That's great.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, and when you talk
about them,

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
are they asking you questions
about your process

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming to jokes
or are you just --

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We just turn on
the microphones.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:11.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You just turn on
the microphones.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
Man what a --
what a tricky thing.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It just flows.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:17.250 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We just talk about it.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just talk about it,
free-associate.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:20.253
-And then you got nice --
I did not know you had

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:23.990
a podcast, but then Judd Apatow
posted this to let everybody

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:24.657 size:88% position:44% line:92%
know you have a podcast.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I never announced that
I was going to have it except

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
Judd Apatow wrote
on his Instagram,

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Doing a podcast
with Mike Birbiglia.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:33.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just told him he has
green veggies stuck between

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
his teeth."

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.469 line:92%
I thought that was really rude.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:42.375
-I'm at this age where my teeth,
they're just, like --

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.177 line:92%
They're just like salad holders.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:47.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just --
When I eat a salad,

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
50% goes in my belly,
40% in my teeth,

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
10% miscellaneous.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're going to have to
track down that miscellaneous.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:57.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
Where's the miscellaneous?

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much
for being here, buddy.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-I can't wait for

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The New Show."
I liked the last five.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
-Mike Birbiglia, everybody!

